# .tetrishrc — tetriSH shell start-up file
# One command per line; blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The shell prepends $PWD/bin to PATH (see init_root), so the daemon and
# system-program binaries under ./bin are found by name.
#
# `dspawn <program> [args...]` daemonises, registers the daemon in
# tmp/daemons.reg, then execs <program>. Inspect running daemons with `dcheck`.
#
# Daemon launch order: the logger first (so it captures everything), then the
# game server, then the optional social layer (the game runs without it).
#
# These daemons are not built yet — uncomment each line as its binary lands:
# dspawn tetrislogd
# dspawn tetrisd
# dspawn marketd
# dspawn chatd
